# Dummy test for debugging purposes
# For use with BatsPP.
## UPDATE 14 Sep 26: Reworked so that intentional failure apparent in batspp output.

# Global setup
# note: Adds output to aid in spotting an intentionally failing test.
$ function my-date { echo "FYI: date changes each second"; command date; }

# This test will pass
# note: The command output is fixed, so it will match recorded cell.
$ echo dummy
dummy

# Another test that always will pass
# note: Added so that a testing glitch doesn't fail entire suite (a la Murphy's Law)
$ echo another dummy
another dummy

# This test will fail: the time will be different when tested
## NOTE: An AI Assistant broke an ealier test by hard-coding the result.
## BAD: echo "Sun Aug  6 11:08:23 PM +0545 2023"
$ my-date
FYI: date changes each second
Fri Sep 25 05:50:33 PM EDT 2026

# End of test (n.b., avoids extraneous new cells after Kernel > Restart ... Run All Cells)

